{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This code snippet very briefly illustrates the 3 core concepts of Vue Query:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../guides/queries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queries"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../guides/mutations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutations"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../guides/query-invalidation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Invalidation"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you're looking for a fully functioning example, please have a look at our "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"basic codesandbox example"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { useQueryClient, useQuery, useMutation } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\n// Access QueryClient instance\nconst queryClient = useQueryClient()\n\n// Query\nconst { isLoading, isError, data, error } = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: getTodos,\n})\n\n// Mutation\nconst mutation = useMutation({\n  mutationFn: postTodo,\n  onSuccess: () => {\n    // Invalidate and refetch\n    queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n  },\n})\n\nfunction onButtonClick() {\n  mutation.mutate({\n    id: Date.now(),\n    title: 'Do Laundry',\n  })\n}\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <span v-if=\"isLoading\">Loading...</span>\n  <span v-else-if=\"isError\">Error: {{ error.message }}</span>\n  <!-- We can assume by this point that `isSuccess === true` -->\n  <ul v-else>\n    <li v-for=\"todo in data\" :key=\"todo.id\">{{ todo.title }}</li>\n  </ul>\n  <button @click=\"onButtonClick\">Add Todo</button>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These three concepts make up most of the core functionality of Vue Query. The next sections of the documentation will go over each of these core concepts in great detail."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis code snippet very briefly illustrates the 3 core concepts of Vue Query:\n\n- [Queries](../guides/queries)\n- [Mutations](../guides/mutations)\n- [Query Invalidation](../guides/query-invalidation)\n\n\n\nIf you're looking for a fully functioning example, please have a look at our [basic codesandbox example](../examples/basic)\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useQueryClient, useQuery, useMutation } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\n// Access QueryClient instance\nconst queryClient = useQueryClient()\n\n// Query\nconst { isLoading, isError, data, error } = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: getTodos,\n})\n\n// Mutation\nconst mutation = useMutation({\n  mutationFn: postTodo,\n  onSuccess: () => {\n    // Invalidate and refetch\n    queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n  },\n})\n\nfunction onButtonClick() {\n  mutation.mutate({\n    id: Date.now(),\n    title: 'Do Laundry',\n  })\n}\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <span v-if=\"isLoading\">Loading...</span>\n  <span v-else-if=\"isError\">Error: {{ error.message }}</span>\n  <!-- We can assume by this point that `isSuccess === true` -->\n  <ul v-else>\n    <li v-for=\"todo in data\" :key=\"todo.id\">{{ todo.title }}</li>\n  </ul>\n  <button @click=\"onButtonClick\">Add Todo</button>\n</template>\n```\n\n\n\nThese three concepts make up most of the core functionality of Vue Query. The next sections of the documentation will go over each of these core concepts in great detail.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: quick-start\ntitle: Quick Start\nref: docs/framework/react/quick-start.md\nreplace: { 'React': 'Vue', 'react-query': 'vue-query' }\n---\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n\nIf you're looking for a fully functioning example, please have a look at our [basic codesandbox example](../examples/basic)\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useQueryClient, useQuery, useMutation } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\n// Access QueryClient instance\nconst queryClient = useQueryClient()\n\n// Query\nconst { isLoading, isError, data, error } = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: getTodos,\n})\n\n// Mutation\nconst mutation = useMutation({\n  mutationFn: postTodo,\n  onSuccess: () => {\n    // Invalidate and refetch\n    queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n  },\n})\n\nfunction onButtonClick() {\n  mutation.mutate({\n    id: Date.now(),\n    title: 'Do Laundry',\n  })\n}\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <span v-if=\"isLoading\">Loading...</span>\n  <span v-else-if=\"isError\">Error: {{ error.message }}</span>\n  <!-- We can assume by this point that `isSuccess === true` -->\n  <ul v-else>\n    <li v-for=\"todo in data\" :key=\"todo.id\">{{ todo.title }}</li>\n  </ul>\n  <button @click=\"onButtonClick\">Add Todo</button>\n</template>\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n"}
